/*
===========================================================================

dhewm3-rt Vulkan — vol_froxel_integrate.comp — froxel column integration.

One invocation per grid COLUMN (x,y).  Walks the Z slices front to back
accumulating Beer-Lambert transmittance and in-scattering — exactly the loop
vol_march.comp runs per screen pixel, done once per column instead.  At the
160x90 default that is 14400 columns against the march's ~500k pixels.

Output (rgba16f 3D image):
  rgb — in-scattering accumulated from the camera to the cell CENTRE
  a   — path transmittance from the camera to the cell CENTRE

Anchored at cell CENTRES, not faces, because the resolve fetches this image
with a trilinear sampler: the sample point of a texel is its centre, so that is
where the stored value has to be correct for interpolation between two texels
to mean anything.  It is also what makes the surface-straddle problem go away
in the resolve — fetching at exactly the surface's depth linearly interpolates
the integral to that depth, which is the fractional weighting of the final
partial cell, for free.

Segment lengths are divided by cos(angle to the view axis): slices are PLANAR,
so the ray length through a cell is longer than the slice's depth extent
everywhere except the exact screen centre.  At a 90-degree horizontal FOV the
screen edge runs ~1.4x, so skipping this would under-integrate the whole
periphery.

Descriptors (set 0):
  binding 0 — froxelScatter rgba16f 3D     (read)
  binding 1 — froxelIntegrated rgba16f 3D  (write)
  binding 2 — VolFroxelParams UBO          (declared by vol_froxel_common.glsl)

20260906_froxel_probe_gi.md Part A, chunk F2.

This file is a new addition with dhewm3-rt.  It was created with the aid of GenAI,
and may reference the existing Dhewm3 OpenGL and vkDoom3 Vulkan updates of the Doom 3 GPL Source
Code.

It is distributed under the same modified GNU General Public License Version 3 of the original Doom 3 GPL Source
Code release.

===========================================================================
*/

#version 460

layout(local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1) in;

layout(set = 0, binding = 0, rgba16f) uniform readonly  image3D froxelScatter;
layout(set = 0, binding = 1, rgba16f) uniform writeonly image3D froxelIntegrated;

#include "vol_froxel_common.glsl"

void main()
{
    ivec2 column = ivec2(gl_GlobalInvocationID.xy);
    ivec3 dims   = max(fp.gridDim.xyz, ivec3(1));
    if (column.x >= dims.x || column.y >= dims.y)
        return;

    // Planar slices -> the ray through this column is longer than the slice
    // depth by 1/cos. Same column centre the fill used, so the two agree.
    vec2  uv    = (vec2(column) + 0.5) / vec2(dims.xy);
    vec3  dir   = vf_RayDirForUV(uv);
    float invZFac = 1.0 / max(dot(dir, fp.camForwardW.xyz), 1e-4);

    vec3  accum = vec3(0.0);
    float trans = 1.0;

    for (int z = 0; z < dims.z; z++)
    {
        vec4  cellData = imageLoad(froxelScatter, ivec3(column, z));
        vec3  inscat   = cellData.rgb; // per unit length, class scales folded in
        float sigma    = max(cellData.a, 0.0);

        float dA = vf_SliceToDist(float(z));
        float dC = vf_SliceToDist(float(z) + 0.5);
        float dB = vf_SliceToDist(float(z) + 1.0);

        // Front half of the cell, up to the centre — that is where the stored
        // value has to land.
        {
            float segLen    = max(dC - dA, 0.0) * invZFac;
            float transAfter = trans * exp(-sigma * segLen);
            // Geometric mean approximates the transmittance at the segment's
            // midpoint rather than at either end — same approximation, and the
            // same reason, as vol_march.comp's stepTransmittance.
            accum += inscat * segLen * sqrt(trans * transAfter);
            trans = transAfter;
        }

        imageStore(froxelIntegrated, ivec3(column, z),
                   vec4(min(accum, vec3(4096.0)), trans));

        // Back half, carried into the next cell.
        {
            float segLen     = max(dB - dC, 0.0) * invZFac;
            float transAfter = trans * exp(-sigma * segLen);
            accum += inscat * segLen * sqrt(trans * transAfter);
            trans = transAfter;
        }

        // No early-out on low transmittance: every texel must be written, or the
        // resolve trilinearly samples whatever the previous frame left behind.
    }
}
